      },
      "message": "ace-ISA-architecture: rework status.ACES\n\n`aceccdirty` is not strictly better than the off/init/clean/dirty model,\nso we can have both, as the customary model is better for optimizing HS\ncontext switches.\nUse the customary model to make ACE more palatable to ARC as well.\n\nRemove ace.enable and ace.disable, since ace.enable serves no clear\npurpose, and ace.disable is a pure context switch optimization.\n\nRename ace.disable to ace.reset, because that is closer to what it does,\nand use an encoding of ace.clean x0, which was originally a functional\nduplicate of ace.clean c0.\n\nAlso mark some surrounding non-normative text as NOTE.",
